# 中频词汇 List03
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2026恋练有词
# 描述: 中频词汇List03核心词汇

constituent /kənˈstɪtjuənt/ n. 成分；选民 Water is a major constituent of the human body. 水是人体的主要成分。
contemplate /ˈkɒntəmpleɪt/ v. 考虑 She contemplated the offer carefully. 她仔细考虑了这个提议。
contention /kənˈtenʃn/ n. 争论 His contention was supported by evidence. 他的论点得到了证据支持。
contradict /ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkt/ v. 矛盾 The findings contradict previous research. 这些发现与之前的研究相矛盾。
controversy /ˈkɒntrəvɜːsi/ n. 争论 The policy generated considerable controversy. 该政策引起了相当大的争论。
convene /kənˈviːn/ v. 召开 Parliament convened to debate the issue. 议会召开会议辩论该问题。
converge /kənˈvɜːdʒ/ v. 趋同 The two trends converge at this point. 两种趋势在这一点上趋同。
correlate /ˈkɒrəleɪt/ v. 相关 Income levels correlate with education. 收入水平与教育相关。
counterpart /ˈkaʊntəpɑːt/ n. 对应物 The German chancellor met with her French counterpart. 德国总理会见了法国同行。
criterion /kraɪˈtɪəriən/ n. 标准 The main criterion for selection is merit. 选拔的主要标准是能力。
curb /kɜːb/ v./n. 抑制 The measures aim to curb inflation. 这些措施旨在抑制通货膨胀。
decisive /dɪˈsaɪsɪv/ adj. 决定性的 The election was a decisive moment in history. 这次选举是历史上的决定性时刻。
dedicate /ˈdedɪkeɪt/ v. 致力于 The foundation dedicates resources to cancer research. 该基金会致力于癌症研究。
default /dɪˈfɔːlt/ n./v. 默认 The system returns to default settings. 系统恢复到默认设置。
deficiency /dɪˈfɪʃnsi/ n. 缺乏 A vitamin deficiency can cause health problems. 维生素缺乏会导致健康问题。
degrade /dɪˈɡreɪd/ v. 降解 Plastics degrade very slowly in the environment. 塑料在环境中降解非常缓慢。
delegate /ˈdelɪɡeɪt/ v./n. 代表 The manager delegated authority to the team leader. 经理将权力下放给了团队领导。
demographic /ˌdeməˈɡræfɪk/ adj. 人口的 Demographic changes affect the labor market. 人口变化影响劳动力市场。
denounce /dɪˈnaʊns/ v. 谴责 The report denounced human rights abuses. 报告谴责了侵犯人权的行为。
deplete /dɪˈpliːt/ v. 消耗 Overuse has depleted the soil of nutrients. 过度使用耗尽了土壤中的养分。
depict /dɪˈpɪkt/ v. 描述 The novel depicts the struggles of ordinary people. 小说描绘了普通人的挣扎。
deploy /dɪˈplɔɪ/ v. 部署 The company deployed new technology across all offices. 公司在所有办公室部署了新技术。
deprive /dɪˈpraɪv/ v. 剥夺 The policy deprives people of their rights. 该政策剥夺了人们的权利。
deteriorate /dɪˈtɪəriəreɪt/ v. 恶化 Relations between the two countries deteriorated. 两国之间的关系恶化了。
deviate /ˈdiːvieɪt/ v. 偏离 The results did not deviate from the expected range. 结果没有偏离预期范围。
differentiate /ˌdɪfəˈrenʃieɪt/ v. 区分 It is important to differentiate between correlation and causation. 区分相关性和因果关系很重要。
dilemma /dɪˈlemə/ n. 困境 The ethical dilemma has no easy solution. 这个道德困境没有简单的解决方案。
diminish /dɪˈmɪnɪʃ/ v. 减少 The importance of traditional media has diminished. 传统媒体的重要性已经降低。
disclose /dɪsˈkləʊz/ v. 披露 Companies must disclose financial information. 公司必须披露财务信息。
discrepancy /dɪˈskrepənsi/ n. 差异 There is a discrepancy between theory and practice. 理论和实践之间存在差异。
